[[:db/retract 17592186124905 :question/answer-fields 17592186122030] {:db/id 17592186124478 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-bcd1cb26-1c44-5d74-aa8e-2093ab435f98"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-bcd1cb26-1c44-5d74-aa8e-2093ab435f98" :question/id #uuid "bcd1cb26-1c44-5d74-aa8e-2093ab435f98" :question/math-academy-id "q-130950" :question/problem "The row echelon form matrix $A$ is given below. What are its **non**-pivot columns?\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}0 & -4 & 3 & -3 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 2 & -6 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 & -3\\end{aligned}]\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Remember that the pivots of a matrix in row echelon form are the first non-zero entries in each row of the matrix.\n\nWe can see that $A$ has $3$ pivots in the $2$nd, $4$th and $5$th columns:\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}0 & -4 & 3 & -3 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 2 & -6 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 & -3\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nTherefore, the only non-pivot columns are the $1$st and $3$rd columns." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-0ec2a6fc-f001-5e94-83d4-c400fba8593b"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-0ec2a6fc-f001-5e94-83d4-c400fba8593b" :answer-field/id #uuid "0ec2a6fc-f001-5e94-83d4-c400fba8593b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-1d3d7552-73fd-5a30-adca-213fce95daf3" :answer-field/choices ["answer-a582f1d6-9082-5ca9-8a15-8892198e09a8" "answer-1d3d7552-73fd-5a30-adca-213fce95daf3" "answer-2c231bf1-1c62-5bb0-a5af-80fd235dc05d" "answer-ab2f5437-3869-5765-88a5-9a58e75de19b" "answer-88eecdfd-f245-5138-93d4-a347d38063c5"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a582f1d6-9082-5ca9-8a15-8892198e09a8" :answer/id #uuid "a582f1d6-9082-5ca9-8a15-8892198e09a8" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$1$st and $2$nd only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-1d3d7552-73fd-5a30-adca-213fce95daf3" :answer/id #uuid "1d3d7552-73fd-5a30-adc